1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Engelborg Strokirk (born June 28, 1691, died April 5, 1715) was a Swedish ironworks heiress and the first wife of prominent industrialist Bengt Gustaf Geijer. She belonged to the prominent Strokirk family from Värm
2 CONC land, Sweden.Life and FamilyBirth: Born in Filipstad, Sweden, on June 28, 1691.Parents: Daughter of mill owner (brukspatron) Henrik Evertsson Strokirk (1652–1700) and Christina Andersdotter Bratt af Brattfors (1658–1731).Marriage:
2 CONC  Married Bengt Gustaf Geijer on May 8, 1709, in Filipstad.Children: Had children including Henrik Geijer (1710–1752) and Christina Engel Geijer (1713–1781).Death: Died on April 5, 1715, at age 23 at Bosjö bruk in Sunnemo, Värmland
2 CONC , shortly after childbirth (in barnsäng). Through her first marriage, ownership ties to Bosjö ironworks were established
2 CONT
2 CONT Gift 8/5 1709 Död i barnsäng  5/4 1715
2 CONT
