1 NAME Friedrichus /Hein/
2 GIVN Friedrichus
2 _MARNM Hein
2 NICK Heine
2 NICK Heinius
1 NAME Friedrich /Hein/
2 GIVN Friedrich
2 SURN Hein
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 MAR 1533
2 ADDR
3 CITY Neubrandenburg
3 STAE Mecklenburg-Vorpommern
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 MAR 1604
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rostock
3 STAE Mecklenburg-Vorpommern
3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU Mecklenburgischer Rat, Bürgermeister in Rostock
1 TITL Mayor
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Friedrich Hein=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Friedrich Hein''', also Friedrich Heine, Friedrich Heinius, born '''March 5, 1533 in Neubrandenburg , † March 18, 1604''' in Rostock was a German legal scholar, university professor and mayor.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Friedrich Hein came''' from an old Neubrandenburg council family. He was born in 1533 as the son of the Neubrandenburg Mayor '''Jacob Hein''' and his wife, the Neubrandenburg mayor's daughter '''Katharina, ''née'' Richard'''. A
2 CONC fter attending school in his hometown, he studied from 1547 at the University of Rostock with '''Arnold Burenius''', then in Frankfurt (Oder) with '''Hieronymus Schurff''' and from 1550 in Wittenberg with '''Philipp Melanchthon'''
2 CONC  and '''Johann Schneidewein'''. In 1553 he attended the university in Leuven. A subsequent educational tripled him to France for four years and then to Italy, where he was awarded a Dr. iur. PhD.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Back in Germany, he''' first worked at the Imperial Court of Justice in Speyer before he was appointed full professor of law (decretals) at Rostock University in 1563/64 by the Duke of Mecklenburg. In 1570 he was appointed to t
2 CONC he Princely Council and also assessor of the newly established consistory. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''In 1574 he gave up''' these offices because "the practical efforts were overloaded". In 1568 and 1574 he was rector of the university. In 1576 he was elected councilor in Rostock and in 1578 after the departure of '''Johannes B
2 CONC orcholten''' to the council syndic of the city. In 1591 he was elected mayor. He held this office until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Friedrich Hein''' was married from 1564 to '''Anna Dobbin''', the daughter of the Rostock councilor '''Albrecht Dobbin'''. The marriage resulted in six sons and five daughters. In a commemorative speech given on March 25, 1605,
2 CONC  which was ascribed to the sons and sons-in-law, the following were named:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Jacobus''' (1565-1634) - Dr. jur. and court court procurator 
2 CONT * '''Albertus''' (1571-1636) - Dr. jur. and professor of decrees 
2 CONT * '''Joannes''' - Canonicus of Bremen Fridericus († 1613) - citizen of Wismar 
2 CONT * '''Fridericus''' († 1613) - Merchant in Wismar
2 CONT * '''Henricus''' (1590-1666) - later professor and rector of the University of Tartu / Dorpat Stephanus (1590-1643) - later a philologist and theologian and the sons-in-law
2 CONT * '''Stephanus''' (1590–1643) – Philologist and theologist
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ernst Cothmann''' (1557-1624) - Dr. jur. utr. and Mecklenburg Council & 1586 '''Elisabetha''' (1566-1642) 
2 CONT * '''Barthold Kichler''' († 1605) - Dr. jur. utr. and Mecklenburg Council & '''Margareta''' (1569-1600)
2 CONT * '''Nikolaus Willebrand''' (1566–1613) - Dr. jur. and Prof. of Ethics & 1596 '''Catharina''' (1576-1662) 
2 CONT  * Marcus Lüschow (1579–1656) - citizen of Rostock, councilor and treasurer & 1602 '''Anna''' († 1607) 
2 CONT * '''Jacob Schabbold''' (Schabbol) - Citizen of Wismar
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
