1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT =Sophia Albertina, Abbess of Quedlinburg=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophia_Albertina,_Abbess_of_Quedlinburg '''Princess Sophia Albertina of Sweden'''] (Sophia Maria Lovisa Fredrika Albertina) was the last [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince-abbot Princess-Abbess] o
2 CONC f [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quedlinburg_Abbey Quedlinburg Abbey], and as such reigned as [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vassal vassal] monarch of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holy_Roman_Empire Holy Roman Empire].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sophia Albertina wa'''s the daughter of King [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adolf_Frederick,_King_of_Sweden '''Adolf Frederick of Sweden'''] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisa_Ulrika_of_Prussia '''Louisa Ulrika of Prussi
2 CONC a''']. She was thus a princess of Sweden, a princess of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duke_of_Holstein-Gottorp Holstein-Gottorp] and a sister to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustav_III_of_Sweden Gustav III of Sweden]. She was a
2 CONC  member of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Accademia_di_San_Luca Accademia di San Luca]. When her brother [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_XIII_of_Sweden '''Charles XIII of Sweden'''] and the rest of the royal family also
2 CONC  became Norwegian royalty in 1814, that did not include Sophia Albertina who then officially was called Royal Princess (of no country).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was given her''' two names as namesake of her two grandmothers: the Prussian Queen [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sophia_Dorothea_of_Hanover '''Sophia Dorothea of Hanover'''] and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess_Albe
2 CONC rtina_Frederica_of_Baden-Durlach '''Margravine Albertina Frederica of Baden-Durlach'''].
