1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Journal Star (Peoria, IL) - Thursday, February 8, 2001 Readability: 3-4 grade level (Lexile: 680L) PEORIA - Elwood L. Sieks , 90, of 2717 W. Edna Court died at 3:45 p.m. Tuesday, Feb. 6, 2001, at OSF Saint Francis 
2 CONC Medical Center. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Nov. 10, 1910, in Peoria to August H. and Bertha I. Ehn Sieks , he married W. Lloyd Drinkwater on March 16, 1946, in Peoria. She survives. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also surviving are one son, Thomas of Peoria; two sisters, Lillian (and Jay) Logue of Commerce, Texas, and Alice (and Gene) Hobaugh of Coral Gables, Fla.; and several nieces and nephews. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was preceded in death by one son, Robert; six brothers; and one sister. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a World War II Army veteran. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the co-owner and operator of Sieks Brothers Grocery Store for 36 years, retiring in 1986. He was a salesman for Bell Clothing Store for 16 years, retiring in 1986. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the Tuesday Club at Neighborhood House. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of Unity Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be at 1 p.m. Saturday at Davison-Fulton Woodland Chapel. Visitation will be from 6 to 8 p.m. Friday at the funeral home. Burial will be in Oak Ridge Cemetery in Camargo. 
