1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Journal Star (Peoria, IL) - Wednesday, January 11, 1995 PEORIA -- Kenneth L. Sieks , 77, of Ocala, Fla., formerly of Peoria, died at 6:45 a.m. Tuesday, Jan. 10, 1995, at Methodist Medical Center in Peoria. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born Jan. 6, 1918, in Peoria to August and Bertha Ehn Sieks , he married Dorothy Stocksick on May 31, 1939, in Peoria. She died Nov. 11, 1986, in Ocala. Three brothers, one sister and two grandchildren also preceded him in death. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are one son, Kenneth R. of Terre Haute, Ind.; three daughters, Judy L. Moretta of Memphis, Tenn., Ellen M. Schultz of Mapleton and Debra L. Surratt of Washington, Ill.; three brothers, Elwood and Melvin, both of Peoria, 
2 CONC and Elmore of Morton; two sisters, Alice Hobaugh of Florida and Lillian Logue of Commerce, Texas; 11 grandchildren; and three great-grandchildren. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a World War II Army veteran. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He retired from Caterpillar Inc. in 1972 as a purchasing agent. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of Morton Knights of Columbus, St. Patrick's Men's Club and the former St. Patrick's Catholic Church in Peoria. He was past president of the Independent Sports Club in Peoria. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of Blessed Sacrament Catholic Church in Morton and St. Jude Catholic Church in Ocala. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Services will be in Ocala at a later date. Burial will be in Forest Lawn Memory Gardens in Ocala. Local visitation will be from 6 to 8 p.m. Friday at Davison-Fulton Woodland Chapel in Peoria. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Memorials may be made to Morton Knights of Columbus. 
