1 NOTE {geni:about_me} MORTON - The Private Funeral Of Richard W. Sieks: Newspaper Obituary and Death Notice Pantagraph, The (Bloomington, IL) - January 24, 1990
2 CONT
2 CONT Deceased Name: MORTON - The Private Funeral Of Richard W. Sieks
2 CONT
2 CONT MORTON - The Private Funeral Of Richard W. Sieks, 65, of Detroit, formerly of Peoria, will be Friday at Knapp-Johnson Funeral Home, Morton. The Rev. Roger Mealiff will officiate. Burial will be in Lutheran Cemetery, Peoria. There 
2 CONC will be no visitation. Mr. Sieks died Sunday afternoon (Jan. 21, 1990) at Harper Hospital, Detroit. He was born July 31, 1924, in Peoria, a son of August and Bertha Ehn Seiks. He married Roxie Lee Barrett June 5, 1972, in Detroit.
2 CONC  She died Aug. 9, 1985. Survivors include five brothers, Elwood and Melvin, Peoria; Fred, Spring Bay; Kenneth, Ocala, Fla.; and Elmore, Morton; two sisters, Alice Hobaugh, Cape Coral, Fla., and Lillian Logue, Commerce, Texas; a st
2 CONC epdaughter, Ann Clay, Detroit; five grandchildren; and 12 great-grandchildren. One brother and one sister preceded him in death. Memorials may be made to the American Heart Association
