1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erik_de_Laval '''''Erik'' Patrik Honoré de Laval'''] was a Swedish modern pentathlete who won a silver medal at the 1920 Summer Olympics.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lieutenant Erik de''' Laval served with the Svea Artillery Regiment (A 1) in Stockholm. He competed at the 1912 Stockholm Olympics together with his elder brothers Georg and Patrik, who were also military officers. Erik was dis
2 CONC qualified in the cross-country riding, while Georg won the bronze medal.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''During World War''' II, de Laval was military attaché at the Swedish Embassy in Poland, and then in Washington. He later wrote books about the modern history of Poland and its leader Józef Piłsudski. In 1948 he served in Damasc
2 CONC us as a member of the UN mission mediating the Arab-Israeli conflict
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/De_Laval_nr_355#TAB_13 '''''Erik'' Patrik Honoré De Laval'''], född 1888-04-28 Stockholm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mogenhetsexamen''' 1906. Volontär vid Svea artilleriregemente 1906. Kadett vid Karlberg 1907. Utexamen 1909. Underlöjtnant vid Svea artilleriregemente 1909. Löjtnant vid Svea artilleriregemente 1914. Genomgick ridskolan å Ström
2 CONC sholm 1912–1913, infanteriskjutskolan 1916 och krigshögskolan 1917–1919. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Stabsadjutant och''' kapten i generalstaben 1923. Kapten i Svea artillerireg, 1923. Biträdande lärare vid artilleri- och ingenjörhögskolan. Kapten i Svea art. reg. s.å. och vid reg.t 1928. RSO 1930, stabsadjudant och kapten vid
2 CONC  generalstaben s.å., överadj. o. major i gen.staben 1931 och vid nämnda stab 1932. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gift 1914-05-02''' i Visby med Elisabet Maria Roos, född 1891-08-22 i Karlskrona, dotter av landshövdingen Gustaf Vilhelm Alexander Roos och Elisabet Maria Charlotta Hedberg.
