0 @I6000000006127446841@ INDI
1 NAME Sofia Amalia /Ribbing/
2 GIVN Sofia Amalia
2 SURN Ribbing
2 _MARNM Ribbing
1 NAME Sofie Ribbing
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 6 MAR 1835
2 PLAC Södraholm
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Adelöv
3 CITY Tranås
3 STAE Småland
3 CTRY Sweden
1 DEAT
2 DATE 7 DEC 1894
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Kristiania
3 CITY Oslo
3 CTRY Norway
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Sofie Ribbing=
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sofie_Ribbing  '''Sofie Amalia Ribbing'''] was a Swedish painter of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C3%BCsseldorf_School Düsseldorf School]. She specialized in portraits and genre scenes, often 
2 CONC placed in family settings.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She was born''' in Adelöv in Jönköping County, Sweden. She was the daughter of Per Arvid Ribbing and Carolina Augusta Ehrencrona. Her father was the Chairman of the local District Court (Häradshövding). When she was only four, 
2 CONC her family moved to Hakarp Parish, closer to Jönköping. Beginning in 1850, she studied at the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Swedish_Academy_of_Fine_Arts Royal Swedish Academy of Fine Arts], then transferred to the [https://
2 CONC en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kunstakademie_D%C3%BCsseldorf Kunstakademie Düsseldorf], where she studied with [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Ferdinand_Sohn '''Karl Ferdinand Sohn'''], who would later become the Academy's President.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She later went to''' Paris and found a position in the studios of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean-Baptiste-Ange_Tissier '''Jean-Baptiste-Ange Tissier'''], then continued her studies in Brussels with the painter and engraver
2 CONC  [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Gallait '''Louis Gallait''']. During the 1860s, she had a studio in Copenhagen. In 1866, under Gallait's sponsorship, she held her first showing at the Brussels Salon. That same year, she had 
2 CONC a successful showing at the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Industrial_Exposition_of_Stockholm_(1866%29 Industrial Exposition of Stockholm]. She later made lengthy visits to London, where she held exhibitions in 1872 and 18
2 CONC 88, and The Hague. She also spent time in Rome with her friend, the painter [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agnes_B%C3%B6rjesson '''Agnes Börjesson''']. She never married. She died during 1894 at Christiania (now Oslo) while visiti
2 CONC ng Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Her works may be''' seen at the Nationalmuseum, Göteborgs konstmuseum and the National Gallery of Norway. In 2016, the Swedish National Heritage Board chose her painting [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boys_Drawing '''Boys Drawi
2 CONC ng'''] (1864) as one of the works that would represent Sweden for "Europeana 280"; a celebration of Europe's shared artistic heritage.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Ribbing_nr_15#TAB_52 '''Sofia Amalia Ribbing'''], född 1835-03-06 på Södraholm i [https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adel%C3%B6vs_socken Adelövs socken]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Studerade målarkonsten''' i Stockholm, Düsseldorf, Paris och Bruxelles. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Död 1894-12-07''' i Kristiania. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bland hennes tavlor''' märkes Ritande gossar (Göteborgs museum).
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT Ur Nordisk Familjebok (1800-talsupplagan)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Ribbing, Sofia Amalia''', den föregåendes kusin, genre- och porträttmålarinna, född i Seminge, Småland, d. 6 Mars 1835, har utbildat sig under studier i Stockholm, Düsseldorf (Sohn), Paris (Tissier) och Bruxelles (Gallait) samt
2 CONC  dessutom längre tider vistats i London och Rom, der hon sedan flere år varit bosatt. Hon har utfört en del genremålningar, såsom Ritande gossar (Göteborgs museum), Trädgårdsmästarens dotter, Fogelboet, Tiggarebarn från Neapel (de
2 CONC  tre sistnämnda utställda i Göteborg 1881) samt flere porträtt. -rn.
