2 CONT * Son of Jörgen (Jöran) Weidling and Katarina Fock
2 CONT * Birth:	1684 in Kalmar, Kalmar Sweden
2 CONT * Death:	January 08, 1716 in Varberg, Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married= 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married:  '''Susanna Hummel'''. Peter relocated to the west coast of Sweden, establishing himself as a prominent merchant and burgher in the port city of Varberg before his early death.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://runeberg.org/gbglund/0067.html Gothenburg nations in Lund members 1669-1906]
2 CONT
2 CONT The first known of the Hummel family was Peter Hummel, who fled to Varberg from Flanders before the Inquisition, where he is said to have belonged to a noble family. He had the children: — AV Hanrns trådman and he part-owner in Va
2 CONC rberg; T 1718), who in his previous marriage became the father of Jacob (101) and in 1700 was remarried in Varberg to the daughter of Påvelsdotter Bravert (b. 1603;  in Varberg 1747); she was widowed by the councillor Antoni Elies
2 CONC on (T 1697), ancestor of the Pvhlson family tse at 275); with Hummel she had a son Hans . 1702; city accountant in Varberg; surveyor in Halmstad 17358; † 1763), married in Halmstad 1733 to Caisa Carelia; — B) Petter (b. 1646; mayo
2 CONC r of Varberg 1690; d. 1709), married first to Susanna Matsdotter and then, in 1693 in Varberg, to the merchant in Halmstad Johan Twist's widow Margreta Kniphof '& 1718); daughters from the mayor Hummel's later marriages were: 1) S
2 CONC uasanna (b. 1694 † 1753), married first in 1712 to the merchant in Varberg Peter Weidling († 1716) and mother of 680, and then in 1717 to the alderman there Nicolanus Gerhard von Deurs i. 1686 † 1755); 2) Johanna (b. 16953 † 1722)
2 CONC , married in 1721 to Johan Pyhlson (4155, who then remarried to her cousin's daughter; — C) Elsa Johanna «b. 1649 † 1683), married to Johan Twist parents of 113); and possibly: — D) Henrik (trader in Halmstad; T 1718), whose widow
2 CONC  died there in 1724.
