1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Based on the information available, it is clear that she belongs to the same family as Hans Andersen Guntzow in Halmstad, Sweden. Together with her husband, she sponsored a school in Halmstad as the family was well
2 CONC  educated. Anders Hansen Guntzow was educated at several universities and became the President of the Court. 
2 CONT
2 CONT How does she fit into the genealogy based on what we know? She is the daughter of Anders but is contemporary with Anders Hansen G. And she cannot be his sister based on the patronyms. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Most likely she is the daughter of an Anders who was Hans Andersen's brother, although we don't have sources for it. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://tidsskrift.dk/personalhistorisk_tidsskrift/article/view/79722/114846
2 CONT
2 CONT 1644 11/4 Andreas Gontzovius, Flensburgensis (Anders Hansen Guntzow, ca. 1621-1696 ,Præsident i Hofretten, imm. 1641 Kbh., 1644 Franeker, 1646 Leyden, 1649 Strassburg)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://tidsskrift.dk/personalhistorisk_tidsskrift/article/view/79732/114856
2 CONT
2 CONT 1646? Jacobus Joh.(Hansen) Guntzowius  synes at være søn af borgmesteren i Halmstad , Hans Andersen Guntzow ,og broder til præsident i hofretten mag. Anders (Hansen) Guntzow
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Hansen Guntzow død 1696. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://tidsskrift.dk/personalhistorisk_tidsskrift/article/view/79809/114933
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Hansen Guntzov (Andreas Joh. Guntzovius), levede siden som Privatmand først i Roskilde og siden i Kjøben-havn. Blev endelig Præsident i Hofretten. Siges at have taget sin Afsked 1695 og at være død 1696.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://finnholbek.dk/pdf/bang.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Mette Jensd . Bang , f. 16 . . oo før 1658 Anders Hansen Guntzow, f. c. 1621 i Halmstad, hvor hans Fader Hans Andersen G., f. 1581, † 3. Jan. 1655, var Borgemester. Hans Moder Bodil Mogensd. † 1658 (begge begravede med Monument
2 CONC  i Roeskilde Domkirke); han dep. 1641 fra Gymnasiet i Lund (tilligemed sin Broder Jacob G.); levede som Privatmand i Kbh., hvor han 1651 tog Magistergraden. Senere blev han Præsident i Hofretten, hvorfra han 1695 tog sin Afsked; †
2 CONC  1696. Han eiede Grimeton i Halland og Rolfstrup. Hans første Kone var Apollone Markusdatter, † 1655. Han oo 3) Maren Grimeton , en D. af Hans Bentsen, Sgp. i Grimeton. Hun gav tilligemed ham, ved Testamente af 13. Oct. 1696, 200 
2 CONC Rd. til Helliggeists K. i Kbh. De ligge begravne i Roeskilde Domkirke. 
